checker_types Summary:
What a pass means: the type of every expression matches upstream's .types baseline, line for line, for every file of the case. The `lines` gradient beside it is the share of individual assertions that match; the walker feeding both agrees with upstream on 97.85% of assertion TEXT, so the residual is the checker rather than the walk
Passed         : 8941/9538 (93.74%)
Assertion lines: 475855/478853 (99.37%)  — a gradient, not a pass rate
Failed         : 597
Skipped        : 2906 (excluded from the denominator)

  1397  skipped: configuration-varied baseline, judged per configuration by checker_types_configured
  135  skipped: the .types baseline has no assertions
  924  skipped: upstream recorded no .types baseline
  450  skipped: upstream records a known divergence from TypeScript

